Multi Gnome Terminal is an enhanced version of gnome-terminal, with
many powerful new features and extensions. The most notable
enhancement is the ability to run multiple terminals within the same
window. Each terminal may be accessed by it's "Tab", through keyboard
shortcuts, or menu selections. Non-active terminals alert that the
buffer has changed, or is changing, with color changes on the Tab
labels. Other enhancements: toolbar, buttonbar, flexible command
configuration to launch new terminals and shells, customizable key
bindings for MGT functions and other uses, shading and tinting,
improved Class handling, font shadowing, and various other
improvements. 

This a major release and has many enhancements with respect to 1.4.x.
Moreover I also fixed several bugs, especially in terminal emulator
support, which is now a real VT102 (passing vttest).

New Features overview:

* SPLITTING
  Now you can have horizontally or vertically split terminals. This
  means that you can create in each Tab several Tabs, splitting
  existing ones.

* TERMINAL BONDING
  Now you can bond terminals so that commands you type are replicated
  to all the bonded terminals.

* VIEWS
  A view is a terminal which accepts no input and which shows 
  output of the "viewed" terminal.

* NEW COMMAND LINE OPTIONS
  There are a number of new command line options. Now you can add
  terminals (new Tabs or hsplit/vsplit) to current MGT window or even
  launch MGT adding new terminals from command line, and even run 
  commands for each terminal being created.

* TEXT SHADOW
  A a very fine outline is drawn around each character when the
  terminal is in "image" mode, improving readability (as Eterm does). 

* ATTACH/DETACH TERMINALS
  You can move a terminal from one Tab to another one, or even
  from one MGT window to another one.


Main bugs fixed:

* selecting a word and then extending selection, word selected got
  lost

* doing 'make menuconfig' and exiting it resulted in terminal screen
  corruption

* doing a "long" ls such as 'ls ~ -R' and interrupting it pressing
  CTRL-C one got bad output.


 Home Page:  http://multignometerm.sourceforge.net

 Downloads:  http://multignometerm.sourceforge.net/web/download.shtml


                                              Cristiano de Michele
 

